    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d166">

                <pb facs="0248" n="234" sameAs="frus:frus1946v06/pg234"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860F.51/11–746: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gallman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-11-07T12:00:00+00:00">November 7,
                        1946—noon.</date><lb/>[Received November 7—8:47 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9336. Mytel 9261, November 5 and 89 to Praha.<anchor n="86" xml:id="d166-f1"/>
                    FonOff official charged Czech Affairs states
                    that when Attlee received Clementis latter immediately introduced question
                    British credits to Czecho and afterwards sought to explain Czech position on US
                    loan declaring “Czech Govt was convinced US action was solely on grounds of
                    Czech attitude at Paris Conference” to which Attlee responded that he was <pb
                        facs="0249" n="235" xml:id="pg235"/> aware that “Secretary Byrnes and others
                    were displeased with the action of Czechs at Paris” and concluded interview by
                    counselling Clementis “upon his arrival in US to take steps at once to come to
                    an understanding with US authorities.”</p>
                <p>Official added interview was very satisfactory from FonOff viewpoint, that Clementis in attitude and approach is
                    typical of Soviet stooges in satellite Govts, and that he is being sent to UN
                    meeting to “keep Masaryk in line.”</p>
                <p>Repeated Praha 91.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gallman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d166-f1" n="86" xml:id="d166-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported that Clementis, who was stopping 3 days in London en
                    route to the United Nations meeting in New York, had paid a widely publicized
                    call on Prime Minister Attlee (860F.51/11–546).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
